<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jami' al-Tawarikh</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Jamiʿ al-Tawarikh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jami">Jami</a>' al-Tawarikh, or Compendium of Chronicles, is a universal history compiled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashid-al-din-hamadani">Rashid al-Din</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a>, in the early fourteenth century. It covers the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> and many other peoples of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eurasia">Eurasia</a> and was richly illustrated. It reflects the scholarly ambitions of Ilkhanid governance.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jami-al-tawarikh.jpg" alt="Jami' al-Tawarikh" width="320" height="312" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rashid al-Din · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mongol_soldiers_by_Rashid_al-Din_1305.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
